I think low-level tools like `strace` or `lsof` often get ignored but help a lot in debugging. They show system calls or open files, which can save hours. But many ignore these because not user-friendly. Could be useful for anyone troubleshooting odd app bugs or performance. 

Warning though—risk of misinterpretation and need some basics knowledge. Always save logs or record findings, so you can reproduce the issue later. Sometimes, simple tools are the most underrated.

